---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Security & Compliance — Veritrail"
  description="SOC 2, GDPR, encryption, hash-chained audit, and BYOK signing keys for Enterprise customers."
>
  <Nav />

  <main>
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="container">
        <h1>Security &amp; compliance</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          Veritrail's product <em>is</em> evidence — so our own security posture has to
          be auditable, not just attested. Here's what we do and how to verify it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="grid-section">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="card-grid">
          <article class="card">
            <div class="status badge-progress">In progress</div>
            <h3>SOC 2 Type II</h3>
            <p>
              We are mid-audit-window with a top-tier auditor for SOC 2 Type II covering
              Security, Availability, and Confidentiality. Type I report available
              under NDA today; Type II expected Q4 2026. Letter of engagement available
              on request to <a href="mailto:security@veritrail.io">security@veritrail.io</a>.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="card">
            <div class="status badge-live">Live</div>
            <h3>GDPR-compliant erasure</h3>
            <p>
              A documented erasure pipeline lets a controller fulfil Article 17 requests
              against any subject-tagged event in the ledger. Erasure preserves the hash
              chain by overwriting only the payload, not the link structure — auditors
              still get a valid chain; the subject still gets their right.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="card">
            <div class="status badge-live">Live</div>
            <h3>Encryption at rest &amp; in transit</h3>
            <p>
              All ingress is TLS 1.3 only. Audit ledger storage is AES-256-GCM with
              per-project data keys wrapped under a region-scoped KMS root.
              Database backups are encrypted with separate keys and stored cross-region.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="card">
            <div class="status badge-live">Live</div>
            <h3>Hash-chained tamper-evident ledger</h3>
            <p>
              Each event includes the SHA-256 hash of the previous event in its project's
              chain. Any insert, delete, or rewrite — by us, by an attacker, or by a
              well-meaning ops team — is detectable at verification time without trusting
              our infrastructure. Roots are published hourly to a public transparency log.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="card">
            <div class="status badge-enterprise">Enterprise</div>
            <h3>BYOK signing keys</h3>
            <p>
              On Enterprise we can sign Receipts with a key you control — held in your
              KMS, your HSM, or an air-gapped offline signer. Veritrail never sees the
              private key; we only ship the signing payload. Loss of Veritrail is no
              longer loss of your evidence chain.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="card">
            <div class="status badge-live">Live</div>
            <h3>Responsible disclosure</h3>
            <p>
              Found something? We pay bounties, we credit researchers, and we don't
              threaten. See <a href="/security.txt"><code>/security.txt</code></a> for the
              latest contact and PGP keys. Median time to first response is under 6 hours.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="cta">
      <div class="container">
        <h2>Need our security package?</h2>
        <p>
          We ship NDA, SOC 2 Type I report, pen-test summary, sub-processor list, and a
          completed CAIQ to any prospect who asks. Email
          <a href="mailto:security@veritrail.io">security@veritrail.io</a> or see
          <a href="/security.txt"><code>/security.txt</code></a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Base>

<style>
  .hero { padding: 4rem 0 2rem; background: linear-gradient(180deg, #f7faff 0%, #ffffff 100%); }
  .lede { font-size: 1.15rem; color: var(--fg-muted); max-width: 680px; margin-top: 1rem; }

  .grid-section { padding: 3rem 0 4rem; }
  .card-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 1.25rem;
  }
  .card {
    padding: 1.5rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: #fff;
  }
  .card h3 { margin: 0.75rem 0 0.5rem; }
  .card p { color: var(--fg-muted); margin: 0; }
  .status {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    padding: 0.2rem 0.55rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
  }
  .badge-live { background: #e6f4ea; color: #0f7c3a; }
  .badge-progress { background: #fff4e0; color: #946100; }
  .badge-enterprise { background: #eaf1fc; color: var(--accent); }

  .cta {
    background: var(--bg-alt);
    padding: 3rem 0;
  }
  .cta p { color: var(--fg-muted); max-width: 680px; }

  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .card-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
</style>
